DAT
id=qid::label=str::text=lstr::
24619::$$$message_0182_0000_0000$$$::                                     He said that the night scares him.::
24620::$$$message_0182_0001_0000$$$::Semina Apartments, Unit 1102, Kurokizaka 4, Shinto.[lr]::
24621::$$$message_0182_0001_0001$$$::That was his apartment.[lr]::
24622::$$$message_0182_0001_0002$$$::His name was...yes, let's call him Mr. A.[lr]::
24623::$$$message_0182_0001_0003$$$::Mr. A, a college student who just turned twenty, moved in during early spring.[lr]::
24624::$$$message_0182_0001_0004$$$::It was the first time he'd ever moved homes, as well as his first time living alone, in a brand new city.[lr]::
24625::$$$message_0182_0001_0005$$$::While the introverted Mr. A had misgivings about his new life, he was slowly adjusting to life in Fuyuki.::
24626::$$$message_0182_0002_0000$$$::He was always comfortable being alone, so it didn't concern him that he had few friends or that there were strangers around him.[lr]::
24627::$$$message_0182_0002_0001$$$::He preferred that, in fact.[lr]::
24628::$$$message_0182_0002_0002$$$::Mr. A tended to hole up in his room, and was rather fond of his new lifestyle where no friends or family would bother him.::
24629::$$$message_0182_0003_0000$$$::He was satisfied with his life,[lr]::
24630::$$$message_0182_0003_0001$$$::except for two things: [lr]::
24631::$$$message_0182_0003_0002$$$::the long, long corridor to his front door,[lr]::
24632::$$$message_0182_0003_0003$$$::and the utter indiscretion of the family that moved in next door one month ago.::
24633::$$$message_0182_0004_0000$$$::He'd had these dissatisfactions, no, worries, since he moved in.[lr]::
24634::$$$message_0182_0004_0001$$$::The apartment his parents found him was practically the size of a single-family home, a XXX,000 yen/month unit with living, kitchen, and dining areas.::
24635::$$$message_0182_0005_0000$$$::It was certainly spacious enough.[lr]::
24636::$$$message_0182_0005_0001$$$::While Mr. A liked solitude, he had expensive tastes, and wouldn't have been happy with modest accommodations.[lr]::
24637::$$$message_0182_0005_0002$$$::The bigger, the better.[lr]::
24638::$$$message_0182_0005_0003$$$::This was his fortress against the outside world.[lr]::
24639::$$$message_0182_0005_0004$$$::A fortress needs to be big and strong. It can't be too easy to reach, and it isn't comfortable unless it's deep enough.::
24640::$$$message_0182_0006_0000$$$::That's right. [lr]::
24641::$$$message_0182_0006_0001$$$::Mr. A didn't necessarily want to be alone.[lr]::
24642::$$$message_0182_0006_0002$$$::He had strangers next to him.[lr]::
24643::$$$message_0182_0006_0003$$$::He was unconsciously afraid of someone invading his safe space.::
24644::$$$message_0182_0007_0000$$$::That was another reason he chose Semina Apartments: [lr]::
24645::$$$message_0182_0007_0001$$$::the distance from the front door to his living room.[lr]::
24646::$$$message_0182_0007_0002$$$::He cared about the distance someone had to cover from his front door to the furthest reaches within, through the corridor you had to cross to leave the apartment.::
24647::$$$message_0182_0008_0000$$$::It was four meters from the living room to the apartment's entrance, with no closets or bathrooms on the way.[lr]::
24648::$$$message_0182_0008_0001$$$::An unusually long floorplan for an apartment, but Mr. A liked it.[lr]::
24649::$$$message_0182_0008_0002$$$::The ideal space and approach.[lr]::
24650::$$$message_0182_0008_0003$$$::The corridor was a vague boundary that made it hard to tell inside from outside, with a distant entrance.[lr]::
24651::$$$message_0182_0008_0004$$$::It was long enough to make one wonder if it was really an "entranceway."::
24652::$$$message_0182_0009_0000$$$::But...[lr]::
24653::$$$message_0182_0009_0001$$$::Ever since he started living there, something bothered him about it.[lr]::
24654::$$$message_0182_0009_0002$$$::At first, he wasn't sure what the problem was, since the length was definitely to his liking, but he finally understood after several months.[lr]::
24655::$$$message_0182_0009_0003$$$::It was very simple;[lr]::
24656::$$$message_0182_0009_0004$$$::the long corridor wasn't lit.::
24657::$$$message_0182_0010_0000$$$::Through some design flaw, there simply wasn't space for a light. Other units had lit entranceways, but 1102 did not.[lr]::
24658::$$$message_0182_0010_0001$$$::He thought it was silly;[lr]::
24659::$$$message_0182_0010_0002$$$::not the builders who forgot to install a light,[lr]::
24660::$$$message_0182_0010_0003$$$::but himself, for not noticing it for months.::
24661::$$$message_0182_0011_0000$$$::   Looking back...[lr]::
24662::$$$message_0182_0011_0001$$$::He'd gotten off on the wrong foot as soon as he failed to realize it.::
24663::$$$message_0182_0012_0000$$$::In the fall, new tenants moved in next door.[lr]::
24664::$$$message_0182_0012_0001$$$::It was a happy family you could find anywhere: [lr]::
24665::$$$message_0182_0012_0002$$$::a young couple with a daughter about three years old. They casually introduced themselves when they moved in.[lr]::
24666::$$$message_0182_0012_0003$$$::All Mr. A knew about this family was that their surname was ____ and their daughter's name was _____.::
24667::$$$message_0182_0013_0000$$$::Semina Apartments was an L-shaped building with two units per floor.[lr]::
24668::$$$message_0182_0013_0001$$$::The entrance was in the middle of the "L", and the perpendicular arms each contained one unit.[lr]::
24669::$$$message_0182_0013_0002$$$::The elevator and emergency exit were at the entrance. Mr. A would occasionally run into the ____ couple, and he would sometimes encounter _____ as well.::
24670::$$$message_0182_0014_0000$$$::"Push the button for me, Mister?"[lr]::
24671::$$$message_0182_0014_0001$$$::She said that every time they met.[lr]::
24672::$$$message_0182_0014_0002$$$::The elevator button was a little bit high for the girl.[lr]::
24673::$$$message_0182_0014_0003$$$::She could reach it if she stretched her arm up high, but for some reason, she never tried to raise her hand above her shoulders.::
24674::$$$message_0182_0015_0000$$$::While he thought it a little strange for a three-year-old girl to go outside by herself, he did what she asked.[lr]::
24675::$$$message_0182_0015_0001$$$::Sometimes he saw her on the first floor, too.[lr]::
24676::$$$message_0182_0015_0002$$$::She would be squatting in front of the elevator when he found her, either leaving or coming home. She would look up at him, have their usual exchange,::
24677::$$$message_0182_0016_0000$$$::and after several such encounters, Mr. A learned the girl's name.[lr]::
24678::$$$message_0182_0016_0001$$$::Of course, he didn't remember her name, because he wasn't interested in other people. She was always wearing a red hoodie, so he called her Little Red Riding Hood. [wm canskip=0]::
24679::$$$message_0182_0017_0000$$$::Again, Mr. A was an introverted young man.[lr]::
24680::$$$message_0182_0017_0001$$$::He didn't care about the outside world, as long as it didn't threaten his lifestyle.[lr]::
24681::$$$message_0182_0017_0002$$$::For example, he could hear arguing through the walls, a little girl crying about twice a day, a woman yelling so loud you couldn't even really call it a scream anymore, the fact that the girl couldn't fully rotate her arm because of an untreated fracture, her father firmly telling her to wear the red hood to hide the bruises on her face... It was none of his business.::
24682::$$$message_0182_0018_0000$$$::Let it not be said that he heard this all just a meter from the front door.[lr]::
24683::$$$message_0182_0018_0001$$$::Anyway, Mr. A's entranceway was very long.[lr]::
24684::$$$message_0182_0018_0002$$$::The shrieks were quite a ways away and he drowned them out with the TV, but otherwise he couldn't do much about it.::
24685::$$$message_0182_0019_0000$$$::One night, however, things got noticeably noisy.[lr]::
24686::$$$message_0182_0019_0001$$$::A shout that could have shattered glass.[lr]::
24687::$$$message_0182_0019_0002$$$::Crying like sirens.[lr]::
24688::$$$message_0182_0019_0003$$$::A door violently being wrenched open, loud enough to reverberate from the 11th floor entrance.[lr]::
24689::$$$message_0182_0019_0004$$$::Thudding noises that could be heard in Mr. A's apartment.::
24690::$$$message_0182_0020_0000$$$::It was 2:00 AM. He was trying to enjoy a late-night program in peace, but that night, it got exceptionally irritating.[lr]::
24691::$$$message_0182_0020_0001$$$::He got up, wishing people would have some common sense.[lr]::
24692::$$$message_0182_0020_0002$$$::Then, he immediately sat back down.[lr]::
24693::$$$message_0182_0020_0003$$$::...It would probably blow over soon enough.[lr]::
24694::$$$message_0182_0020_0004$$$::The domestic environment next door was none of Mr. A's business. He tried not to think about. It wouldn't be good to leave and get himself involved.::
24695::$$$message_0182_0021_0000$$$::He believed in personal responsibility.[lr]::
24696::$$$message_0182_0021_0001$$$::People should solve their own problems, Mr. A thought, as he lifted the remote control and increased the TV volume by five.[lr]::
24697::$$$message_0182_0021_0002$$$::By the time he turned off the TV and went to sleep later that night, it was quiet again.::
24698::$$$message_0182_0022_0000$$$::Mr. A learned the next day that the entire household next door had died in a murder-suicide.[lr]::
24699::$$$message_0182_0022_0001$$$::He was questioned by the police for the first time in his life.[lr]::
24700::$$$message_0182_0022_0002$$$::Last night, the wife [block len=2] murdered the husband with a blunt weapon after a verbal altercation. She went on to kill their daughter with an edged weapon and then took her own life.[lr]::
24701::$$$message_0182_0022_0003$$$::Mr. A told the police that he was asleep and didn't know what happened.[lr]::
24702::$$$message_0182_0022_0004$$$::As the police officer politely thanked him and was about to leave, Mr. A asked a question.::
24703::$$$message_0182_0023_0000$$$::"Um, what happened to the daughter?"[lr]::
24704::$$$message_0182_0023_0001$$$::The officer's eyebrows slightly quirked up, answering,[lr]::
24705::$$$message_0182_0023_0002$$$::"Her blood was on the murder weapon, so we know she was stabbed. Based on the bloodstains, we believe it was a lethal wound."[lr]::
24706::$$$message_0182_0023_0003$$$::But then, the young officer continued[lr]::
24707::$$$message_0182_0023_0004$$$::in an uncomfortable whisper.::
24708::$$$message_0182_0024_0000$$$::"But there's no body. We couldn't find it anywhere.[lr]::
24709::$$$message_0182_0024_0001$$$::It wasn't in the room, or near the floor entrance she ran out to."::
24710::$$$message_0182_0025_0000$$$::The story was simple.[lr]::
24711::$$$message_0182_0025_0001$$$::After Little Red Riding Hood was attacked by her mother, she escaped to the 11th floor entrance.[lr]::
24712::$$$message_0182_0025_0002$$$::But there were no other traces of her after that.[lr]::
24713::$$$message_0182_0025_0003$$$::Her blood trail ended at the elevator.::
24714::$$$message_0182_0026_0000$$$::"I don't know why she didn't use the elevator.[lr]::
24715::$$$message_0182_0026_0001$$$::Actually, why didn't she go to her neighbor for help? Even if she was in a state of panic, she could have pushed the doorbell."::
24716::$$$message_0182_0027_0000$$$::Mr. A didn't answer that the buttons would have been too high for her to reach in either case.::
24717::$$$message_0182_0028_0000$$$::The officer left, leaving Mr. A to his thoughts at his front door.[lr]::
24718::$$$message_0182_0028_0001$$$::He imagined the girl running from her mother in a panic past the floor exit to his front door, frantically pounding on the door at 2:00 AM. [lr]::
24719::$$$message_0182_0028_0002$$$::In the end,[lr]::
24720::$$$message_0182_0028_0003$$$::they never found the little girl's body.::
24721::$$$message_0182_0029_0000$$$::Days later...[lr]::
24722::$$$message_0182_0029_0001$$$::Mr. A noticed an odd noise at the same time, every night.[lr]::
24723::$$$message_0182_0029_0002$$$::It was very soft, low enough that you had to strain to hear it.[lr]::
24724::$$$message_0182_0029_0003$$$::Whatever it was, he didn't think about it for a while. He was convinced it was the wind coming through his windows.::
24725::$$$message_0182_0030_0000$$$::The noise came every night.[lr]::
24726::$$$message_0182_0030_0001$$$::[font italic=true]Knock, knock.[font italic=false][lr]::
24727::$$$message_0182_0030_0002$$$::It was so small it sounded like it would fade any second, but it grated on him.[lr]::
24728::$$$message_0182_0030_0003$$$::Once he realized it was coming from the front door and not the window, [move textoff=0 time=600 path=(400,260,255)(400,260,0) storage=fk025台詞b accel=0]Mr. A...[lr]::
24729::$$$message_0182_0030_0004$$$::walked down his long corridor to the front door.::
24730::$$$message_0182_0031_0000$$$::"Who's there?" he asked over the intercom.[lr]::
24731::$$$message_0182_0031_0001$$$::There was no answer.[lr]::
24732::$$$message_0182_0031_0002$$$::The sound was so quiet. Once Mr. A arrived at his front door, [textoff][noise opacity=160][se volume=100 storage=se637.wav][wait canskip=0 time=2000][stopnoise][texton]::
24733::$$$message_0182_0032_0000$$$::he checked the peephole.[lr]::
24734::$$$message_0182_0032_0001$$$::Through the round, distorted field of view, he couldn't see anyone at the entrance.[lr]::
24735::$$$message_0182_0032_0002$$$::But there were some red spots on the beige floor[line len=2]::
24736::$$$message_0182_0033_0000$$$::His eardrums were about to burst. There was no one at the entrance. [quake vmax=8 hmax=5 time=1500][se volume=100 storage=se637.wav]The noise wouldn't stop. [condoff target=all][noise_back][rep force=1 textoff=0 fliplr=0 tops=0 storages=fk026覗き窓 time=400 flipud=0 lefts=0 bg=fk027マンション内装c indexes=3000]Mr. A's eyeball approached the peephole again. There could have been someone there, but he was at the wrong angle to see them. [quake vmax=8 hmax=5 time=1500][se volume=100 storage=se637.wav]The noise wouldn't stop. It was right below the peephole. Something just out of view...[lr]::
24737::$$$message_0182_0033_0001$$$::Something wearing red was stuck to the door...[quake vmax=8 hmax=5 time=1500][se volume=100 storage=se637.wav]::
24738::$$$message_0182_0034_0000$$$::He ran back down the long corridor.[lr]::
24739::$$$message_0182_0034_0001$$$::The clock read 2:00 AM.::
24740::$$$message_0182_0035_0000$$$::This had become a nightly visit.[lr]::
24741::$$$message_0182_0035_0001$$$::The sound came every night.[lr]::
24742::$$$message_0182_0035_0002$$$::Mr. A refused to open the door.[lr]::
24743::$$$message_0182_0035_0003$$$::The sound came tonight, too.[lr]::
24744::$$$message_0182_0035_0004$$$::It was quiet enough to dismiss as his imagination,[lr]::
24745::$$$message_0182_0035_0005$$$::but it was also sharp and agonizing, like a knife in his brain.::
24746::$$$message_0182_0036_0000$$$::Day by day, Mr. A's mind was driven into a corner.[lr]::
24747::$$$message_0182_0036_0001$$$::Fall ended.[lr]::
24748::$$$message_0182_0036_0002$$$::He started to hear the sound at any time of day.[se volume=50 storage=se637.wav][lr]::
24749::$$$message_0182_0036_0003$$$::One night, he made up his mind.[lr]::
24750::$$$message_0182_0036_0004$$$::He would see who was at the door.::
24751::$$$message_0182_0037_0000$$$::He walked down the long corridor.[lr]::
24752::$$$message_0182_0037_0001$$$::A bit of light filtered through the frosted glass of the door.[lr]::
24753::$$$message_0182_0037_0002$$$::Crossing the long, unlit corridor,[lr]::
24754::$$$message_0182_0037_0003$$$::he pushed the door open.::
24755::$$$message_0182_0038_0000$$$::There was nobody there.[lr]::
24756::$$$message_0182_0038_0001$$$::He couldn't hear the ear-grating, skull-pounding knock.[lr]::
24757::$$$message_0182_0038_0002$$$::Of course. There's no way that would happen. There was never a noise or red hood to begin with.[lr]::
24758::$$$message_0182_0038_0003$$$::Haha, ha, ha.[lr]::
24759::$$$message_0182_0038_0004$$$::His laugh was tinged with relief.[lr]::
24760::$$$message_0182_0038_0005$$$::His chilled body quickly regained its warmth.::
24761::$$$message_0182_0039_0000$$$::He was just hearing things.[lr]::
24762::$$$message_0182_0039_0001$$$::That incident must have bothered him a lot more than he realized.[lr]::
24763::$$$message_0182_0039_0002$$$::He'd started to feel guilty and deluded himself into feeling responsible.[lr]::
24764::$$$message_0182_0039_0003$$$::That wouldn't happen anymore.[lr]::
24765::$$$message_0182_0039_0004$$$::Everything was over, now that he'd opened the door.::
24766::$$$message_0182_0040_0000$$$::Phew.[lr]::
24767::$$$message_0182_0040_0001$$$::He wiped the sweat from his forehead and closed the door.[lr]::
24768::$$$message_0182_0040_0002$$$::As he turned the lock, he looked up.[lr]::
24769::$$$message_0182_0040_0003$$$::In front of him,[lr]::
24770::$$$message_0182_0040_0004$$$::in the long, dark corridor [se volume=30 storage=se637.wav]he liked so much...::
24771::$$$message_0182_0041_0000$$$::His pupils widened.[lr]::
24772::$$$message_0182_0041_0001$$$::In the middle of the corridor, there was something.[lr]::
24773::$$$message_0182_0041_0002$$$::                                 A familiar-looking dead body,[lr]::
24774::$$$message_0182_0041_0003$$$::wearing a red hood,::
24775::$$$message_0182_0042_0000$$$::seemed to be pleading for something.[lr]::
24776::$$$message_0182_0042_0001$$$::Mr. A was sure, without knowing why, that he'd die if he listened.[lr]::
24777::$$$message_0182_0042_0002$$$::The dark lips opened,[lr]::
24778::$$$message_0182_0042_0003$$$::like a watermelon split by a knife.[lr]::
24779::$$$message_0182_0042_0004$$$::With bloody lips, Little Red Riding Hood asked,::
24780::$$$message_0182_0043_0000$$$::[delay speed=10]                                              "[delay speed=180]Mister, [wait canskip=0 time=800]push the..."[wvs][delay speed=user][wait time=800][r]::
24781::$$$message_0182_0043_0001$$$::"Punch punch punch punch![rf][lr]::
24782::$$$message_0182_0043_0002$$$::What the heck, that was so lame! And why'd you have to make it so dramatic? Honestly! Too many details, Mitsuzuri! You put too much effort into the acting! And the story's too long![lr]::
24783::$$$message_0182_0043_0003$$$::What's wrong with this Mr. A, anyway!? If things get that bad, just move! Move out, bro...!"[wvs][clfg textoff=0 time=100 storage=082_マッキーパンチ]::
24784::$$$message_0182_0044_0000$$$::October 11th, shortly after noon, in the Ryudou Temple training camp room.[lr]::
24785::$$$message_0182_0044_0001$$$::Makidera's strange voice pierces the autumn evening.::
24786::$$$message_0182_0045_0000$$$::"If it were that easy, everyone would move.[lr]::
24787::$$$message_0182_0045_0001$$$::How many years have you been saying you're going to run away?[lr]::
24788::$$$message_0182_0045_0002$$$::People always choose familiarity over the unknown.[lr]::
24789::$$$message_0182_0045_0003$$$::If everyone moved over a little ghost, this island would be uninhabited."::
24790::$$$message_0182_0046_0000$$$::"Hm, that's quite profound. Ghost stories really are something we'll always be attached to, even if we try not to be.[lr]::
24791::$$$message_0182_0046_0001$$$::By the way, Makino-G. How fares the drink-pouring geisha in your long hallway?"::
24792::$$$message_0182_0047_0000$$$::"She doesn't exist! We don't have anyone that fancy in our house! [cacheimage storage=蒔寺私服04b(中)][wvl][chgfg textoff=0 pos=c time=300 storage=蒔寺私服04b(中)]We also don't get any water dropping in the halls at night when it isn't raining, okay!? And none of my ancestors were Setouchi pirates!"[lr]::
24793::$$$message_0182_0047_0001$$$::"Ah-ha, right, I just remembered your house is pretty old, Makidera. What, did the hallway story hit a nerve? Is this one of your weaknesses?"::
24794::$$$message_0182_0048_0000$$$::"Shut up! I'm not afraid of hallways! Besides, [font italic=true]I[font italic=false] want to move to a new fancy apartment![lr]::
24795::$$$message_0182_0048_0001$$$::...Wait, what do you mean, 'hit a nerve'? Is that a new chakra?"::
24796::$$$message_0182_0049_0000$$$::"...How do you know what a chakra is but not 'hit a nerve'?[lr]::
24797::$$$message_0182_0049_0001$$$::You might've heard of the 'demon gate' in superstition. The demon gate is also an idiom for a weakness, ergo when Mitsuzuri said 'hit a nerve,'[cacheimage storage=一成私服03b(中)][wvl][chgfg textoff=0 time=200 storage=一成私服03b(中)] she meant that..."::
24798::$$$message_0182_0050_0000$$$::Issei Ryudou.[lr]::
24799::$$$message_0182_0050_0001$$$::Issei is the son of the temple's head monk and the student council president at school.[lr]::
24800::$$$message_0182_0050_0002$$$::His job made him the chaperone of this club training camp, and he's been glancing this way.::
24801::$$$message_0182_0051_0000$$$::"Huh. You sure know your stuff, temple boy.[lr]::
24802::$$$message_0182_0051_0001$$$::But no thanks. What I want to ask about is more cosmic stuff. Ghost stories and the like are just barking up the wrong tree."::
24803::$$$message_0182_0052_0000$$$::"Y'know, something more realistic, like a meteorite falling on Tohsaka's house during the Edo period, or a secret giant cave under Fuyuki."::
24804::$$$message_0182_0053_0000$$$::"I thought that story was realistic enough.[lr]::
24805::$$$message_0182_0053_0001$$$::In the true crime version of that story, was the true culprit Mr. A all along, and he hid the girl's body in his hallway's walls...or something like that?"::
24806::$$$message_0182_0054_0000$$$::"Um... Kane, I think that misses the point of a ghost story."::
24807::$$$message_0182_0055_0000$$$::"You want something more realistic? What do you think a ghost story is supposed to be?[lr]::
24808::$$$message_0182_0055_0001$$$::Tall tales are Tohsaka's specialty. She'll tell you some good ones if you're patient."::
24809::$$$message_0182_0056_0000$$$::"That won't happen. I don't know any stories that Miss Makidera would like."::
24810::$$$message_0182_0057_0000$$$::Rin Tohsaka answers elegantly.[lr]::
24811::$$$message_0182_0057_0001$$$::She tends to act this way during group outings such as these.[chgfg opacity=0 textoff=0 time=100 storage=美綴私服01a(中)]::
24812::$$$message_0182_0058_0000$$$::"Well, excuse me. What about you, Matou? One of the first years said that Captain Matou is really scary despite her looks."::
24813::$$$message_0182_0059_0000$$$::"M-me!? [cacheimage storage=桜私服03e(中)][wvl canskip=0 time=400][chgfg textoff=0 time=300 storage=桜私服03e(中)]I d-don't really like scary stories, though I don't mind hearing them...[lr]::
24814::$$$message_0182_0059_0001$$$::By the way, who told you that?"[lr]::
24815::$$$message_0182_0059_0002$$$::"...Haah. You don't even realize that's the scary part of you, Sakura..."::
24816::$$$message_0182_0060_0000$$$::Rin murmurs.[lr]::
24817::$$$message_0182_0060_0001$$$::Nobody else here knows that Rin Tohsaka and Sakura Matou are siblings.::
24818::$$$message_0182_0061_0000$$$::"It's fine to take a break, but we've only just started.[lr]::
24819::$$$message_0182_0061_0001$$$::Will we keep going or not? I'm of a mind to call off this entire meeting if Makidera doesn't settle down."::
24820::$$$message_0182_0062_0000$$$::"Yeah, wouldn't want to bother the sleeping monks. We'll continue if Makidera promises to stop shouting."[lr]::
24821::$$$message_0182_0062_0001$$$::"I'm not [font italic=true]loud[font italic=false]. I was just expressing my disapproval at Mitsuzuri's lame story."[cacheimage storage=凛私服05b(中)][wvs][fg textoff=0 opacity=0 left=-324 index=4000 top=45 time=100 storage=凛私服05b(中)]::
24822::$$$message_0182_0063_0000$$$::"The problem is her criticism that comes afterward. Asking Miss Makidera to be patient is like telling her not to breathe. You might as well give up.[lr]::
24823::$$$message_0182_0063_0001$$$::What do you think, Miss Makidera? Could you hold your breath?"::
24824::$$$message_0182_0064_0000$$$::"I could. My next best sport after running is swimming."[lr]::
24825::$$$message_0182_0064_0001$$$::"So you have it. Let's continue. Miss Saegusa is next, I think."::
24826::$$$message_0182_0065_0000$$$::"R-right! Ah... But I've never told a scary story, um..."[lr]::
24827::$$$message_0182_0065_0001$$$::"It's okay, you don't have to try and scare us.[lr]::
24828::$$$message_0182_0065_0002$$$::Ayako was just being mean-spirited by dramatizing a true story. Miss Makidera got scared because she knows the actual story of Semina Apartments."::
24829::$$$message_0182_0066_0000$$$::"R-really?"[lr]::
24830::$$$message_0182_0066_0001$$$::"Mm-hm. The family suicide actually happened. About a month later, the person next door went missing, and they're still looking for them."::
24831::$$$message_0182_0067_0000$$$::"Stooop! Stop it right nooooww! [cacheimage storage=蒔寺私服01f(近)][wvl][chgfg textoff=0 time=200 storage=蒔寺私服01f(近)]I'm sure Mr. A had his reasons for going on a journey of self-discovery! Some special reason! [cacheimage storage=蒔寺私服04b(近)][wvl][chgfg textoff=0 time=200 storage=蒔寺私服04b(近)]One day, he'll come back all grown up![lr]::
24832::$$$message_0182_0067_0001$$$::You've got some nerve making up a weird reason for that cool guy to disappear, Ayako Mitsuzuri!"::
24833::$$$message_0182_0068_0000$$$::"Huh... D-did Mr. A really go missing?"[lr]::
24834::$$$message_0182_0068_0001$$$::"Yes, according to another building resident. Right, O Lady Mitsuzuri?"::
24835::$$$message_0182_0069_0000$$$::"That's what they said.[lr]::
24836::$$$message_0182_0069_0001$$$::It's still spooky enough, even without dramatizing it.[lr]::
24837::$$$message_0182_0069_0002$$$::Makidera's such a scaredy-cat. You should attack with a similar approach, Miss Saegusa. Do you know any ghost stories you've heard from someone else?"::
24838::$$$message_0182_0070_0000$$$::"Oh, I do know a few. Um, have you all heard of the window ghost?[cacheimage storage=蒔寺私服01g(中)][wvl][movefg textoff=0 opacity=255 left=-53 top=30 time=600 accel=-2 storage=蒔寺私服01g(中)] It's a rumor that started going around during our second term..."::
24839::$$$message_0182_0071_0000$$$::"What's that? News to me."[lr]::
24840::$$$message_0182_0071_0001$$$::"The shadow at the haunted mansion, right? I heard the kyudo club first-years talking about it."::
24841::$$$message_0182_0072_0000$$$::"Yes, that haunted mansion.[lr]::
24842::$$$message_0182_0072_0001$$$::According to the rumor, there's this vacant mansion somewhere in Fuyuki, and if you go near it at night, you can see a silhouette staring at you from a second floor window."[lr]::
24843::$$$message_0182_0072_0002$$$::"Huh? What kinda silhouette, Yukicchi? And what part of Fuyuki is this mansion at?"::
24844::$$$message_0182_0073_0000$$$::"I don't know... But it must be a place people don't approach often.[lr]::
24845::$$$message_0182_0073_0001$$$::Apparently someone's actually seen it before, after they got lost and stumbled across the house. There's trees all around it, there aren't any people nearby, and the ghost on the second floor is a woman."::
24846::$$$message_0182_0074_0000$$$::"A woman all alone in an abandoned mansion? Sounds like Tohsaka's house.[lr]::
24847::$$$message_0182_0074_0001$$$::Tohsaka, they're talking about your place like a haunted house!"[lr]::
24848::$$$message_0182_0074_0002$$$::"Uh... I-I guess? I'm sorry, Miss Tohsaka. Is this about your house?"::
24849::$$$message_0182_0075_0000$$$::"Don't apologize, Miss Saegusa. This isn't the first time I've heard such rumors about my neighborhood."::
24850::$$$message_0182_0076_0000$$$::It's not exactly slander.[lr]::
24851::$$$message_0182_0076_0001$$$::The Tohsaka estate is, in fact, a type of haunted house.::
24852::$$$message_0182_0077_0000$$$::"Th-then I'll talk about Shinto instead![lr]::
24853::$$$message_0182_0077_0001$$$::Umm, lately at night, you can see what looks like a big string in the sky above Shinto..."::
24854::$$$message_0182_0078_0000$$$::Yukika Saegusa looks around timidly.[lr]::
24855::$$$message_0182_0078_0001$$$::......From the looks of it, she's checking for eyewitnesses.::
24856::$$$message_0182_0079_0000$$$::"...I heard it was like a string. Has anyone seen it?"[lr]::
24857::$$$message_0182_0079_0001$$$::"I've heard the rumor, but unfortunately, I've yet to encounter such a sight."::
24858::$$$message_0182_0080_0000$$$::"In the sky at night? [cacheimage storage=凛私服09a(中)][wvl][chgfg textoff=0 time=300 storage=凛私服09a(中)]...Um, you don't mean they saw someone standing on top of the Center Building, right?"::
24859::$$$message_0182_0081_0000$$$::"Ah-ha, how specific. I've heard that rumor of a red silhouette on top of the Center Building a lot, but you're talking about something else, right, Miss Saegusa?"[cacheimage storage=凛私服12b(中)][wvs][chgfg textoff=0 time=300 storage=凛私服12b(中)]::
24860::$$$message_0182_0082_0000$$$::...Ayako Mitsuzuri gives them an inscrutable gaze.[lr]::
24861::$$$message_0182_0082_0001$$$::Rin Tohsaka smiles uncomfortably. She often prefers wearing red clothes.[lr]::
24862::$$$message_0182_0082_0002$$$::It's already been half a year since the Fifth Holy Grail War ended.[lr]::
24863::$$$message_0182_0082_0003$$$::Is she still going out on patrol at night?::
24864::$$$message_0182_0083_0000$$$::"Have you seen it?"[lr]::
24865::$$$message_0182_0083_0001$$$::"Nope. It was probably a UFO!"[lr]::
24866::$$$message_0182_0083_0002$$$::"I read that too, you know.[lr]::
24867::$$$message_0182_0083_0003$$$::Makidera, you've got the wrong idea about ghost stories."::
24868::$$$message_0182_0084_0000$$$::"Yes, what we're discussing is the occult, not the cosmic.[lr]::
24869::$$$message_0182_0084_0001$$$::Makino-G, I'm afraid that the Moo-Moo topic you enjoy so much isn't going to come up."::
24870::$$$message_0182_0085_0000$$$::"Gah. I d-d-don't know what you're talking about. I never bought a weird rag like that! I bet it's really boring, even if it exists!"[lr]::
24871::$$$message_0182_0085_0001$$$::"That boring aspect of it is exquisite in its own way, though.[lr]::
24872::$$$message_0182_0085_0002$$$::By the way, with regard to the topic of the mirage above Shinto..."::
24873::$$$message_0182_0086_0000$$$::Everyone shakes their heads.[lr]::
24874::$$$message_0182_0086_0001$$$::Unfortunately no one here has witnessed it.[lr]::
24875::$$$message_0182_0086_0002$$$::However...[lr]::
24876::$$$message_0182_0086_0003$$$::What is this feeling I've been having for a while...?::
24877::$$$message_0182_0087_0000$$$::"...I have another rumor to share.[lr]::
24878::$$$message_0182_0087_0001$$$::You've heard the story of the old castle in the forest outside town, I assume? There's a new story about it.[lr]::
24879::$$$message_0182_0087_0002$$$::Apparently, if you enter the forest and walk towards the castle, a ghost from the Imperial Army will appear and spirit the visitor away to the battlefield."::
24880::$$$message_0182_0088_0000$$$::"Only by overcoming several trials can the hero spend the night at the phantasmal castle under the care of a pair of maid sisters."::
24881::$$$message_0182_0089_0000$$$::"Ryudou? Did you pray so hard that your brain melted?"[lr]::
24882::$$$message_0182_0089_0001$$$::"Q-quiet, you! I know how strange it sounds! But someone has actually seen it, so I was just sharing! If you don't believe me, go attempt it yourself!"::
24883::$$$message_0182_0090_0000$$$::Wow, that um...[lr]::
24884::$$$message_0182_0090_0001$$$::Wow.[lr]::
24885::$$$message_0182_0090_0002$$$::It sounds kinda interesting.::
24886::$$$message_0182_0091_0000$$$::"What about you, Emiya? What do you think of Ryudou's rumor?"[lr]::
24887::$$$message_0182_0091_0001$$$::Mitsuzuri turns to me. I've been silent this whole time.[lr]::
24888::$$$message_0182_0091_0002$$$::Man, I couldn't come up with any remarks, so I was keeping to myself, but...::
24889::$$$message_0182_0092_0000$$$::"Well, Issei wouldn't make things up. Ryudou Temple is close to the forest, so it might actually be real."[lr]::
24890::$$$message_0182_0092_0001$$$::It's not exactly implausible, either.[lr]::
24891::$$$message_0182_0092_0002$$$::...And I hate to interrupt, but I suddenly remember I need to use the toilet.::
24892::$$$message_0182_0093_0000$$$::"Sorry, gotta go to the bathroom. I'll try to slip back in without interrupting, so go on without me.[lr]::
24893::$$$message_0182_0093_0001$$$::I'll try to look for the right timing to give Makidera a good scare."::
24894::$$$message_0182_0094_0000$$$::"Grgh...! H-hmph! Fine, bring it on![lr]::
24895::$$$message_0182_0094_0001$$$::I'm a woman, so I won't lose to you, Emiya."::
24896::$$$message_0182_0095_0000$$$::She gives me a bizarre reaction, as always.[lr]::
24897::$$$message_0182_0095_0001$$$::Makidera's been saying that kind of stuff to me ever since I started having lunch with Tohsaka at school.::
24898::$$$message_0182_0096_0000$$$::The night chill hits my skin once I step outside.[lr]::
24899::$$$message_0182_0096_0001$$$::The air in the mountains is colder and sharper than in the city.[lr]::
24900::$$$message_0182_0096_0002$$$::My foggy head and indistinct thoughts, steeped in the cold, awaken as a distinct entity.::
24901::$$$message_0182_0097_0000$$$::"...Whew."[lr]::
24902::$$$message_0182_0097_0001$$$::I look up at the night sky and heave a sigh.[lr]::
24903::$$$message_0182_0097_0002$$$::I've already walked twenty meters from the room we were all in.[lr]::
24904::$$$message_0182_0097_0003$$$::I'm in the corridor crossing the temple. Contemplation without any goal in mind is a fresh experience all its own.::
24905::$$$message_0182_0098_0000$$$::"Now, then..."[lr]::
24906::$$$message_0182_0098_0001$$$::What should I think about?[lr]::
24907::$$$message_0182_0098_0002$$$::I guess I'll go over how I got into this situation.[lr]::
24908::$$$message_0182_0098_0003$$$::The most recent event would be the training camp today.[lr]::
24909::$$$message_0182_0098_0004$$$::It stemmed from the cultural festival coming up soon, Sakura working hard as the kyudo club captain, Mitsuzuri watching over her, and our strange relationship with the track & field club.::
24910::$$$message_0182_0099_0000$$$::After some twists and turns, we gradually settled on holding this joint training camp to prepare for the cultural festival.[lr]::
24911::$$$message_0182_0099_0001$$$::Issei lent us a space, and I was invited as manual labor. I'm just the cook.::
24912::$$$message_0182_0100_0000$$$::My days have been pretty busy lately, but they've also been undoubtedly peaceful ones.[lr]::
24913::$$$message_0182_0100_0001$$$::I think back to half a year ago,[lr]::
24914::$$$message_0182_0100_0002$$$::to the Holy Grail War and everything that happened.[lr]::
24915::$$$message_0182_0100_0003$$$::It was a war where I both lost and gained something.[lr]::
24916::$$$message_0182_0100_0004$$$::Enough time has passed that I can calmly reminisce on it.::
24917::$$$message_0182_0101_0000$$$::The Holy Grail War is all in the past.[lr]::
24918::$$$message_0182_0101_0001$$$::Fuyuki is free of any sparks of conflict.[lr]::
24919::$$$message_0182_0101_0002$$$::The Holy Grail is gone. The Servants are no longer among us. The dead won't walk again. Time flows on without a hitch.::
24920::$$$message_0182_0102_0000$$$::My daily life doesn't need to change.[lr]::
24921::$$$message_0182_0102_0001$$$::They're all here, the various factors connecting each of my days.[lr]::
24922::$$$message_0182_0102_0002$$$::The right way for a human to live is by enjoying the slight changes bridging yesterday to today, and today to tomorrow.::
24923::$$$message_0182_0103_0000$$$::"...Ahh..."[lr]::
24924::$$$message_0182_0103_0001$$$::My thoughts grind to a halt.[lr]::
24925::$$$message_0182_0103_0002$$$::There was another reason I'm at this camp, I think...::
24926::$$$message_0182_0104_0000$$$::"...What's that?"[lr]::
24927::$$$message_0182_0104_0001$$$::I just spotted something standing in the corner of my eye.[lr]::
24928::$$$message_0182_0104_0002$$$::...It's in the temple courtyard. I couldn't see it clearly from this far away, but a human-like silhouette was running into the woods.[lr]::
24929::$$$message_0182_0104_0003$$$::I...[wait canskip=1 time=3000]::
24930::$$$message_0182_0105_0000$$$::...It must be one of the temple monks.[lr]::
24931::$$$message_0182_0105_0001$$$::We aren't the only people at Ryudou Temple.[lr]::
24932::$$$message_0182_0105_0002$$$::I think someone is in the courtyard, but worrying about it won't get me anywhere.::
24933::$$$message_0182_0106_0000$$$::"...Right, yeah. Anyway, where's the toilet..."[lr]::
24934::$$$message_0182_0106_0001$$$::I pick up the pace and jog down the corridor, when...[lr]::
24935::$$$message_0182_0106_0002$$$::Just as I'm rounding the corner, I crash into someone.::
24936::$$$message_0182_0107_0000$$$::"Ah, sorry..."[lr]::
24937::$$$message_0182_0107_0001$$$::"I apologize. I wasn't paying attention."[lr]::
24938::$$$message_0182_0107_0002$$$::"..."[lr]::
24939::$$$message_0182_0107_0003$$$::My brain grinds to a halt.[lr]::
24940::$$$message_0182_0107_0004$$$::I'm so surprised, I don't even know what I'm surprised about.::
24941::$$$message_0182_0108_0000$$$::"But you should watch where you're going.[lr]::
24942::$$$message_0182_0108_0001$$$::It's reckless to run in the hallways, boy."::
24943::$$$message_0182_0109_0000$$$::Caster keeps going.[lr]::
24944::$$$message_0182_0109_0001$$$::She's as refined and sardonic as always, but it's rare to see her uncovered face.[lr]::
24945::$$$message_0182_0109_0002$$$::But if I had to say what really surprised me...[lr]::
24946::$$$message_0182_0109_0003$$$::"...Yeah. Caster's incredibly beautiful."[lr]::
24947::$$$message_0182_0109_0004$$$::I resume my brain functions by talking to myself and continue walking.::
24948::$$$message_0182_0110_0000$$$::I empty my mind.[lr]::
24949::$$$message_0182_0110_0001$$$::I'll finish my business and go back to the camp room.::
24950::$$$message_0182_0111_0000$$$::"...And thus did Yahachi return to life, resurrected by his mother's mad desire to reunite with her son that the villagers drove to death.[lr]::
24951::$$$message_0182_0111_0001$$$::But the arisen Yahachi was missing a few things. He had no arms, legs, heart, or brain.[lr]::
24952::$$$message_0182_0111_0002$$$::To make up for what he lost, Yahachi's mother would kidnap villagers and take the parts from them..."::
24953::$$$message_0182_0112_0000$$$::Issei's eyes are shining.[lr]::
24954::$$$message_0182_0112_0001$$$::Temple boy, indeed. Once you bring up graves, dead bodies, and karmic retribution, no one knows more than he does.[lr]::
24955::$$$message_0182_0112_0002$$$::Everyone is glued to the story in rapt silence, waiting for the shoe to drop. Makidera, of course, but even Himuro, Mitsuzuri, and Tohsaka, who seem like they'd have a high tolerance for horror stories.[lr]::
24956::$$$message_0182_0112_0003$$$::Everyone's wearing the same expression.[lr]::
24957::$$$message_0182_0112_0004$$$::...I wonder if something odd just happened.::
24958::$$$message_0182_0113_0000$$$::Even Mr. Kuzuki is quietly listening to Issei's story.[lr]::
24959::$$$message_0182_0113_0001$$$::As for Fuji-nee, our leader...[lr]::
24960::$$$message_0182_0113_0002$$$::"Why do you think a tiger is strong?[wvs][wait canskip=0 time=600][lr]::
24961::$$$message_0182_0113_0003$$$::It's because they learn that 'scary stories' aren't actually scary. You kids are weak against stories like that, so you need to train yourselves against them."::
24962::$$$message_0182_0114_0000$$$::So she said, on the verge of tears, and went off to bed early.[lr]::
24963::$$$message_0182_0114_0001$$$::Our faculty chaperone is skipping out on her job.[lr]::
24964::$$$message_0182_0114_0002$$$::Still, it wouldn't do for a bunch of boys and girls our age to have a secret meeting in the dark, so she pushed her responsibility onto Mr. Kuzuki.::
24965::$$$message_0182_0115_0000$$$::"That's how Yahachi became a thinking dead man. Tragically, by the time he could say his mother's name again, she had already passed away, consumed by her evil sorcery.[lr]::
24966::$$$message_0182_0115_0001$$$::Yahachi mourned. He wasn't happy to be alive again. Still, his mother had endured great suffering to bring him back to life, so he couldn't wallow in self-pity."::
24967::$$$message_0182_0116_0000$$$::"Yahachi decided he would try to resurrect his mother, like she did for him... But no matter how many times he tried, he failed.[lr]::
24968::$$$message_0182_0116_0001$$$::He followed his mother's wicked arts to the letter, using as much blood and flesh from the villagers as it took, but his mother would not come back to life."::
24969::$$$message_0182_0117_0000$$$::"W-why not? The z-z-zombies are trying to reproduce. I feel bad for them, so just let them multiply![lr]::
24970::$$$message_0182_0117_0001$$$::What's wrong with one more zombie mom, or even ten?[lr]::
24971::$$$message_0182_0117_0002$$$::Also why are you talking like that, President?"::
24972::$$$message_0182_0118_0000$$$::"Stop interrupting, Makidera! The way I'm speaking is a Ryudou family tradition."::
24973::$$$message_0182_0119_0000$$$::"Ahem.[lr]::
24974::$$$message_0182_0119_0001$$$::It stands to reason that Yahachi and his mother were of different positions, in a spiritual sense. There was a rule that could not be broken, no matter what demonic or sorcerous arts he used."::
24975::$$$message_0182_0120_0000$$$::"Only the living can raise the dead.[lr]::
24976::$$$message_0182_0120_0001$$$::The dead can consume the dead to increase their numbers, but they can never bring them back to life.[lr]::
24977::$$$message_0182_0120_0002$$$::The product is not human, but a ghoul that exists only to feed on the dead."::
24978::$$$message_0182_0121_0000$$$::...He has a point.[lr]::
24979::$$$message_0182_0121_0001$$$::The dead can't make wishes come true. You can only do that while you're alive.[lr]::
24980::$$$message_0182_0121_0002$$$::Even if the dead are granted a new lease on life, the dead absolutely can't raise the dead.[lr]::
24981::$$$message_0182_0121_0003$$$::That's always been true.[lr]::
24982::$$$message_0182_0121_0004$$$::Only the living have the role of summoning the dead.::
24983::$$$message_0182_0122_0000$$$::"Failing to understand this truth, Yahachi kept gathering flesh. It's said that even now, he hoards human limbs in the dragon cave, hoping to resurrect his mother.[lr]::
24984::$$$message_0182_0122_0001$$$::That is the legend of Yahachirou of the Corpse Mound, and the supposed origin of the Organ Graveyard of Kageyama."::
24985::$$$message_0182_0123_0000$$$::Issei finishes his story.[lr]::
24986::$$$message_0182_0123_0001$$$::A candle goes out.[lr]::
24987::$$$message_0182_0123_0002$$$::It's someone else's turn to tell a tale.::
24988::$$$message_0182_0124_0000$$$::"...That one was pretty heavy. I didn't think the son of the head priest would talk about graveyards while we're sleeping over at the temple.[lr]::
24989::$$$message_0182_0124_0001$$$::I have to applaud your bad taste."::
24990::$$$message_0182_0125_0000$$$::"Hmph. You're on my turf today.[lr]::
24991::$$$message_0182_0125_0001$$$::I'll use any means I have to exterminate the enemies of Buddhism."::
24992::$$$message_0182_0126_0000$$$::Who's up next?[lr]::
24993::$$$message_0182_0126_0001$$$::We're doing the time-honored camp tradition of telling scary stories in a circle.::
24994::$$$message_0182_0127_0000$$$::"Come on, Emiya. You're up next.[lr]::
24995::$$$message_0182_0127_0001$$$::I know the president's performance is a hard act to follow, but give us the best you got."[lr]::
24996::$$$message_0182_0127_0002$$$::"I wouldn't worry about that.[lr]::
24997::$$$message_0182_0127_0003$$$::Senpai is good with scary stories. He gave Ms. Fujimura quite the scare over the summer."::
24998::$$$message_0182_0128_0000$$$::All eyes turn to me.[lr]::
24999::$$$message_0182_0128_0001$$$::...I know a scary story or two, but it's my first time telling one in front of this many people.[lr]::
25000::$$$message_0182_0128_0002$$$::Telling stories isn't really my thing, to begin with.[lr]::
25001::$$$message_0182_0128_0003$$$::I can't really spice them up, and I can't even tell if they're interesting or not.::
25002::$$$message_0182_0129_0000$$$::"Just relax, Emiya.[lr]::
25003::$$$message_0182_0129_0001$$$::Try to imagine we're in the shed."::
25004::$$$message_0182_0130_0000$$$::...You're gonna make me blush.[lr]::
25005::$$$message_0182_0130_0001$$$::...Oh, well.[lr]::
25006::$$$message_0182_0130_0002$$$::It's not my thing, but we're having a party.[lr]::
25007::$$$message_0182_0130_0003$$$::In order to cap off the most fun camp I've ever been to...[lr]::
25008::$$$message_0182_0130_0004$$$::"...Here's a long one, then."[lr]::
25009::$$$message_0182_0130_0005$$$::...I'll step out of character and tell a story for the first time.::
924954::$$$message_9182_0112_0001$$$::Temple boy, indeed. Once you bring up graves, dead bodies, and karmic retribution, no one knows more than he does.[r]::��